      "text": "To convert the point \\((\\rho, \\theta, \\phi) = \\left( 3, \\frac{5 \\pi}{12}, 0 \\right)\\) from spherical coordinates to rectangular coordinates \\((x, y, z)\\), we use the following transformation formulas:\n\n\\[\nx = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\cos \\theta\n\\]\n\\[\ny = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\sin \\theta\n\\]\n\\[\nz = \\rho \\cos \\phi\n\\]\n\nGiven:\n\\(\\rho = 3\\), \\(\\theta = \\frac{5 \\pi}{12}\\), and \\(\\phi = 0\\)\n\nFirst, we calculate \\(\\sin \\phi\\) and \\(\\cos \\phi\\):\n\n\\[\n\\sin \\phi = \\sin 0 = 0\n\\]\n\\[\n\\cos \\phi = \\cos 0 = 1\n\\]\n\nNext, we substitute these values into the formulas for \\(x\\), \\(y\\), and \\(z\\):\n\n\\[\nx = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\cos \\theta = 3 \\cdot 0 \\cdot \\cos \\left( \\frac{5 \\pi}{12} \\right) = 0\n\\]\n\n\\[\ny = \\rho \\sin \\phi \\sin \\theta = 3 \\cdot 0 \\cdot \\sin \\left( \\frac{5 \\pi}{12} \\right) = 0\n\\]\n\n\\[\nz = \\rho \\cos \\phi = 3 \\cdot 1 = 3\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the rectangular coordinates are:\n\n\\[\n(x, y, z) = (0, 0, 3)\n\\]\n\nPutting the final answer in \\(\\boxed{}\\):\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{(0, 0, 3)}\n\\]",
